        "text_preview": "\nHowever, the learned trial court as well as the learned Appellate Court has not contemplated the above parameters of the Act 2006, which are mandatory."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6c2b018718d148aa9861897fdabd5c14_24",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "As per the law laid down, the learned Trial Court as well as the Appellate Court are bound to consider the effect of said misbranding on human life."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "20b614718bb94f12a74ca8a5ceefd6ce_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Learned Courts below have not given any finding regarding the fact that due to the misbranding."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b5345dda00844327b581f4c0491317bb_26",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "the food sample has become unsafe for human consumption."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a88cb8bd636c4699beaf25ae5ebac7b3_27",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "On this aspect, the law laid down in the case of Nemi Chand vs State of Rajasthan (2016) 2 AICLR 479 and the case of Harish Dayani Vs. State of Madhya Pradesh 2020 (M.P.) 144 and also the case of Purushottam Vs.\nState of Madhya Pradesh (CRR"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0f9ef60a8f2442c88467b5372c99f45d_28",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "9. On due consideration of the rival submissions so also the facts and circumstances of the case, this Court is of the view that both the Courts below have not committed any error in appreciation of evidence available on record."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b4ab3aafa6444940bf9eb239a9825d8a_29",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Hence, no infirmity is found in the impugned order passed by both the Courts below, accordingly, the same is upheld."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "76c4ec5cd8e44fcca6d81f0e2875b5db_30",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "However, looking to the submissions of the learned counsel for the petitioner, this Court is of the view that the fine amount imposed against the petitioner be reduced from Rs. 2,00,000/- to Rs.50,000/- ."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c1b0d990863f4dbb9855820415d1bee8_31",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
